# CI executes scripts/*.sh directly, and so do contributors on WSL and Git
# Bash. A CRLF checkout turns `set -euo pipefail` into a syntax error, so pin
# shell scripts to LF. This is deliberately scoped rather than applying
# `* text=auto eol=lf` globally, which would rewrite the working tree of every
# existing contributor on their next checkout for no benefit.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the documented Windows entry point; CRLF is correct for it.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
